; A source line holding CONTROL BYTES, quoted under a caret by the human
; renderer. The quoted line is echoed to a terminal, and it went out raw:
; the ESC in the string below wrote `[31m` - red - into the report, a
; colour `style.ax` did not choose, and a NUL, backspace or carriage
; return mid-line moves or hides what the caret points at. The MESSAGE
; surfaces escaped such bytes since 2026-08-16 (478-json-control-bytes);
; the quoted source line did not. Found 2026-09-27 from the seeded
; fuzzer's control-byte edits.
;
; Each control byte is drawn as its Unicode CONTROL PICTURE now - ESC as
; U+241B, SOH as U+2401, DEL as U+2421 - one column wide, like the byte
; it stands for, so the caret under `undefinedHere` still lands on it. A NUL
; is drawn the same way (U+2400) but cannot sit in a fixture: this
; harness reads lines through bash, which drops it. The same code path
; draws it, and scripts/check-fuzz.sh holds every refusal's human report
; to "no raw control byte" over mutants that insert NULs.
(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (let ((s "red:[31mXY")) undefinedHere))
